{{Quote|I, uh, used to work on Coruscant&hellip;at a ship factory&hellip;of new ships.''"<br />"''A factory job on Coruscant? You expect us to believe you graduated from the Mechanic's Academy?''"<br />"''Mechanic's Aca&mdash; ha! No! No, no, no, no, no. I'm self-taught.|Kazuda Xiono and Tamara Ryvora|audio=MechanicsAcademy-TheTripleDark.flac|<ref name="The Triple Dark" />}}
The '''Mechanic's Academy''' was an academy for [[Technician|mechanics]].<ref name="The Triple Dark" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{ResistanceDate|1|3}}</ref> during his [[Mission on the Colossus platform|mission]] on the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]'' on the [[planet]] [[Castilon]], the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] told his fellow mechanics [[Tamara Ryvora]] and [[Neeku Vozo]] that he had worked in a [[Starship|ship]] [[factory]] on<ref name="The Triple Dark" /> the planet<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Coruscant]] beforehand in order to keep his true affiliation a secret. The claim prompted Ryvora to ask if he expected them to believe he had graduated from the Mechanic's Academy, which Xiono stated was not the case and that he was instead self-taught.<ref name="The Triple Dark" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Mechanic's Academy was first mentioned in "[[The Triple Dark]],"<ref name="The Triple Dark" /> the third episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which premiered on [[October 14]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref>

